WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.213
AI operations starts with two questions.

00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:05.113
What did a task cost?

00:00:05.113 --> 00:00:07.260
And did it do the job well enough?

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.227
Workbench brings those answers together before you change models.

00:00:11.227 --> 00:00:16.656
Let's follow a subscription-support task from captured usage to a justified routing review.

00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:20.907
A clean workspace starts without application data.

00:00:20.907 --> 00:00:23.323
The screen explains how to begin.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:27.885
For this walkthrough, we explicitly load the recorded support example.

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:32.321
The cases are fictional, and the model responses were saved earlier.

00:00:32.321 --> 00:00:35.605
No new model calls are made during this demonstration.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:44.671
The overview shows twenty-four tickets compared across three models: seventy-two task runs and one hundred forty-four captured calls.

00:00:44.671 --> 00:00:48.309
Their recorded API estimate is about nine cents.

00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:52.087
This is a saved comparison, not a company invoice.

00:00:52.087 --> 00:00:56.963
Missing prices stay unknown, and hardware and electricity remain unmeasured.

00:00:57.833 --> 00:01:00.714
Open the refund-inside-the-window task.

00:01:00.714 --> 00:01:08.405
Workbench shows the customer request and the calls behind it: classify the request, then draft the decision and reply.

00:01:08.405 --> 00:01:10.920
Each step has its captured cost.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.610
Call completed means the API returned successfully.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.201
Answer quality still needs evaluation.

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:24.030
For your own application, create an AxonLLM source and configure its scoped connector.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:27.708
A durable outbox retries unacknowledged usage.

00:01:27.708 --> 00:01:33.574
The feed contains metadata, while saved answers are imported separately for quality checks.

00:01:33.574 --> 00:01:38.875
The recorded example is clearly labeled as a saved source, not a live connection.

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:41.854
Now run the evaluation.

00:01:41.854 --> 00:01:48.928
Workbench replays saved answers against the subscription-support contract and real Ostiari Guard checks.

00:01:48.928 --> 00:01:52.303
It checks policy decisions and action boundaries.

00:01:52.303 --> 00:01:57.733
The worker continues in the background, and the result remains available after you leave the page.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:05.407
The result compares tickets passed, critical failures, recorded response time, and cost per passing ticket.

00:02:05.407 --> 00:02:09.072
Money spent on failed tickets is included in that cost.

00:02:09.072 --> 00:02:11.801
These checks grade the saved responses.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:17.032
They do not establish today's model quality or performance on unrelated workloads.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.971
Set the requirements before looking for savings.

00:02:20.971 --> 00:02:25.129
With the saved strict criteria, no model qualifies.

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:29.557
Workbench explains each exclusion instead of inventing a winning model.

00:02:29.557 --> 00:02:32.985
The next decision is to investigate the failing cases.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:37.388
Export the review with its evidence; no production route has been changed.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:41.417
The interactive architecture connects the pieces.

00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:44.660
AxonLLM supplies captured calls.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:47.375
Workbench owns the ledger and review.

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:51.753
The worker and Ostiari Guard evaluate saved evidence.

00:02:51.753 --> 00:02:54.769
Select a component or play a narrated flow.

00:02:54.769 --> 00:02:59.531
Small solid circles show the direction, with pause and reduced-motion controls.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:07.709
Administrators can inspect evaluation-service health, queued work, failed evaluations, and calls without a price.

00:03:07.709 --> 00:03:13.653
The recorded demo is not new application traffic, so these recent-traffic counts can be zero.

00:03:13.653 --> 00:03:19.360
Company operators configure retention, backups, monitoring, and their response process.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:31.814
The optional AWS hosted test uses separate seeded and clean stacks, real Cognito sign-in, private CloudFront origins, encrypted off-host backups, and alarm receipts.

00:03:31.814 --> 00:03:34.464
Its architecture is interactive too.

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:41.713
This is a single-host test, with an explicit no-MFA exception, not a high-availability production guarantee.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:52.440
Workbench makes one complete decision path visible: connect usage, inspect a task, evaluate saved answers, and review the model choice with evidence.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:57.903
Explore the source, run the recorded demo, and connect your own application when you are ready.
